# SABOTAGE: the aggregate's STATUS. `aggregate/2` is the whole point of the fleet command — a
# roll-up whose `status` is a real function of its members. Dropping the `Enum.all?` makes the
# fleet report `"ok"` whenever the roster is non-empty, so a FAILED verifier (or an unevaluable
# one) reads as a green fleet and a CI job keying on the aggregate's status is told nothing is
# wrong while a member is red. The document still parses, still counts, and `verifiers` still
# carries the failing entry — nothing catches this except an assertion on the TOP-LEVEL status,
# which is exactly what a dashboard keys on.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/verify_fleet_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: ONE failing member makes the whole fleet fail
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/verifier/fleet.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/verifier/fleet.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/verifier/fleet.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/verifier/fleet.ex
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@
   """
   @spec aggregate(Path.t(), [map()]) :: map()
   def aggregate(root, documents) when is_list(documents) do
-    ok? = documents != [] and Enum.all?(documents, &(&1["status"] == "ok"))
+    ok? = documents != []
 
     %{
       "task" => @task_name,
